{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"USN-8939-1","published":"2026-10-19T17:17:18Z","modified":"2026-10-19T23:43:25.831517708Z","upstream":["CVE-2016-7951","CVE-2016-7952","CVE-2026-94286","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-7951","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-7952","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-94286"],"summary":"libxtst vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain RECORD\nreplies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this\nissue to cause libXtst clients to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-94286)\n\nTobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain\nmemory operations. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to\ncause libXtst to access memory out of bounds, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7951)\n\nTobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain\nreplies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this\nissue to cause libXtst to enter an infinite loop, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7952)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libxtst","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libxtst?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:1.2.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]}],"versions":["2:1.2.2-1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libxtst6","binary_version":"2:1.2.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-8939-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libxtst","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:18.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libxtst?arch=source&distro=esm-infra%2Fbionic"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:1.2.3-1ubun